  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe real Jarvis design doc lives at `doc/subsystems/jarvis-mode.md`; references written as `doc/jarvis-mode.md` (missing the `subsystems/` segment) point to a non-existent path. This PR normalizes the **source-doc** references to the canonical path and fixes the 3 genuinely broken hyperlinks with location-correct targets so they actually resolve on GitHub.\n\n## What changed (20 files)\n\n- `doc/**` (subsystems / local / main / specs / api / adr / deprecated)\n- `README.md`, `README.zh-CN.md`, `DELIVERY.md`\n- `services/scripts/sync-docs.py` (docstring example), `services/scripts/stop-windows.ps1` (comment)\n- `services/kws-training/README.md`\n\n### Hyperlink fixes (must resolve)\n- `README.md:64` / `README.zh-CN.md:64` → `[doc/subsystems/jarvis-mode.md §14](doc/subsystems/jarvis-mode.md)` (root-relative)\n- `doc/deprecated/700809-raw-extract.md:12` → `[../subsystems/jarvis-mode.md](../subsystems/jarvis-mode.md)` (resolves from `doc/deprecated/`)\n\n### Text-reference normalization\n- All inline `doc/jarvis-mode.md` / bare `jarvis-mode.md` / `../jarvis-mode.md` strings → `doc/subsystems/jarvis-mode.md` (canonical root-relative, matching how `delivery/UserStory.md` already cites it).\n\n## Scope discipline\n- **Excluded** generated/historical docs: `delivery/`, `reports/`, `archive/` (and `doc/README.md` was already correct).\n- **Excluded** descriptive mentions without a `.md` path (doc-name lists, \"jarvis-mode 解析失败\" notes, runtime `jarvis-mode.log`).\n- No logic changes; markdown/prose/comment only.\n\n## Prerequisite\n- The 3 webui **code-comment** references were fixed separately in **PR #10** (`server.py`, `jarvis_routes.py`, `joy_ws.js`). This PR closes the remaining doc-side references.\n\n## Verification\n- Grep of the 20 changed files shows zero remaining `doc/jarvis-mode.md`, bare `jarvis-mode.md`, or `../jarvis-mode.md`.\n- `git diff --stat` = exactly the 20 intended files (unrelated `.gitignore` working-tree change deliberately left out of the commit).",
